  "notes": "The Thug/Gunna-orbit architect, and the research defines him by contrast: \"brighter and more consonant than the 808 Mafia lane\". Everything here is that comparison made numeric. `halfStepDissonance` drops to 0.05 and `chordToneBias` rises to 0.78 where the dark bench sits at 0.3 and 0.5; `extensions` is the lushest in this batch (ninth 0.35 over triad 0.25) for the m9 and add-11 the research names, voiced `open` across 52–86; the 808 is clean with no distortion and `glideProb` 0.75, the slowest deliberate glides here. The drums are restrained rather than hard — `kick.densityPerBar` [2,4] and `syncopation` 0.3 — and the mid-range that the dark bench leaves empty is filled by percussion instead, which is why `percs.lanes` carries shaker, tambourine and rim at [2,4] a bar, the busiest perc lane in this batch. Melody is a high arpeggio over a chord bed, so `countermelody` leads with `arp` at `densityRatio` 0.55 and `phraseBars` reaches 8. Bridges drop the drums. ⚠ `medium` because the research rates it high-medium. The inferred parameters are the drum numbers — \"restrained\" and \"tasteful\" are the paragraph's only words for them — and the i–iv–VII–III family, which is INFERRED; the research names no numerals for him, only \"4-bar progressions with pad-and-pluck voicings\".",
